{"verdict": "supported",
  "answer": "The evidence states that the TRF2-RTEL1 interaction is mediated by a metal-coordinating C4C4 motif in RTEL1, which is required for TRF2 to recruit RTEL1 to telomeres in S phase. Disruption of this interaction by the RTEL1(R1264H) mutation or the TRF2(I124D) substitution abolishes RTEL1 binding, confirming the C4C4 motif's role. The claim is directly supported by the cited excerpts.",
